Thu Nov 05 14:56:20 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Use larger read buffers on vsock connections

  For a higher throughput larger buffers on the data path are set.
  The three copy loops now use a 64 KiB buffer instead of 1 byte,
  set by a new IO_BUFFER_SIZE constant. Along with the buffers
  retries are faster. Vsock Connect-back loop now retry every
  100 ms instead of every 1s. Also stream_listener now creates
  its socket before starting its thread, so it exists when the
  command goes to the VM. Before, if sci connected back first,
  it had to wait a full 1s for its next retry.

