Mon Nov 02 14:09:17 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add access checking for open_dir

  Opening the rootfs and the optional layers needs to be more
  strict. After opening R_OK | X_OK is required. faccessat2 syscall
  runs directly on the opened descriptor with:

  - AT_EMPTY_PATH checks the directory the descriptor refers to
  without looking the path up again, so the path can't be swapped
  between open and check.

  - AT_EACCESS is essential: the helper's real UID stays root
  (only the effective IDs are switched), so without it every
  check would pass.

  The checks happens with the caller's identity, prior any
  privileges gain

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Nov 02 12:31:23 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fixes on read_config_file

  Make sure to open a registration file such that it does not
  block on FIFO's. After open check that the file is still a
  regular file and reject if not. Last check that the filesize
  does not exceed a certain limit. Currently we set 1MB which
  is way more than a simple yaml registration files should
  ever need.

