Thu Oct 29 15:08:27 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add --user option to flake-ctl firecracker register

  The new option names the user to call the application as
  inside of the VM. flake-ctl stores it as user in the runtime
  section of the registration and firecracker-pilot passes it
  to the guest as sci_user=NAME on the kernel commandline. The
  name is validated on both sides such that it cannot break up
  the kernel commandline.

  sci looks up the user in /etc/passwd and /etc/group of the
  instance and calls the command with the user and group ID
  and the supplementary groups of the user, for the console as
  well as for the vsock based calls. The databases are read
  directly instead of using NSS, because a statically linked
  sci cannot load the NSS modules of the glibc in the instance.
  If the user does not exist in the instance a warning is
  printed in debug mode and the command is called as root.
  The setting is ignored for a command which replaces sci as
  the init process, e.g systemd.

  Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

