Wed Oct 28 20:46:33 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Drop flake-pilot helper sandbox-run

  The sandbox-run helper received all options including
  the command to call inside of the sandbox as options
  to the helper binary. With this approach the call cannot
  be strictly mapped in a sudoers definition. Therefore
  the sandbox-run helper was droped and a new helper named
  bubblewrap-pilot was added. The new helper only receives
  the path of the pilot registered app and the user provided
  caller options for the command. The helper reads the
  associated registration options from the app registration
  and has now all information to call the bwrap

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 18:09:46 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add comment why tmpfs is attached before overlay

  The tmpfs is created before the overlay because an
  overlay refuses upper, work and lower directories of
  a detached mount, and nothing can be attached into a
  detached mount (up to Linux 6.14)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 18:03:59 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Clear the group when switching back from layers

  Split the identity switch out of open_layers_as() into two helpers
  for better readability. open_layers_as is now three steps: switch
  to the caller, open the layers, switch back. Switching back always
  happens, even after a partial switch.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 17:08:51 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix potential infinite loop from caller_groups

  The open-ended loop is now for _ in 0..MAX_GROUP_READS.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 16:44:17 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix the open_user_dir check

  open_root_owned_dir() only checks that each component belongs to
  root. It doesn't check that the components are not writable by
  others, or are sticky. If /var/tmp were mode 0777 without the
  sticky bit, another user could rename bwrap_<uid> and put their
  own directory or symlink in its place. The owner check wouldn't
  stop that, because it only covers the directory that was opened.
  This can't give anyone root, since bwrap runs without privileges,
  but it would compromise the caller's sandbox. This commit
  fixes it by require each component to be not writable by others

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 16:28:56 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Guard open_layers

  Just before calling open_layers(), it checks that the effective
  user and group IDs are exactly the caller's. If not, it refuses
  with an error and switches back to root as usual.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 26 09:28:16 CET 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Refactor build and deployment workflow

  Add build and deployment metadata files. Instead of creating
  a full build script for each app build, only provide the caller
  options to the respective flake-ctl podman|firecracker build
  commands. Next to this add metadata to deploy the built images
  to an ECR or S3.

  Consequently a tool per appstore is implemented to build and
  deploy the container or image blobs. All shell scripts to build
  and push data has been removed.

