Thu Oct 22 09:42:51 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Better error handling for unregistered pilot

  Running a pilot binary directly no longer panics. Instead
  a clear error message and exit code is raised. Each pilot
  loads its registration first thing in main(), but registration::load_config()
  panicked instead of returning an error. So calling a pilot
  binary directly aborted with a core dump, and so would a
  flake whose registration is gone or whose YAML is broken.

