Wed Oct 21 15:30:03 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Bump version: 3.2.9 → 3.2.10

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 14:34:51 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Make sure bubblewrap holds no host mounts

  The current version of the bubblewrap-pilot manages the
  root of the bwrap in overlay mounts below /var/tmp/bwrap_UID
  This leaks the contents of the host root directory to a
  location which allows others to read usually root private
  data which is a security issue. The proposed fix operates
  in two conditions:

  1. if the rootfs and layers have no mount points below them,
  the pilot sets everything up itself in its own namespace.

  2. Mount points below, e.g. /: the pilot hands over to a new
  helper command, sandbox-run, via sudo. The helper builds
  the mounts as root in a private mount namespace, then drops
  to your user for good, sets no_new_privs, and starts bwrap
  there. Nothing is mounted on the host on either path.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 13:01:10 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

