Wed Oct 21 11:57:50 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix EOF wait in firecracker-pilot

  The pilot reads just the exit status line and no longer waits
  for the end of the stream.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 11:14:22 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix handling of resume and force_vsock options

  The runtime options resume and force_vsock were used at
  registration time to create the VM cmdline boot_args
  sci_resume and sci_force_vsock. Changing the runtime
  options only without the boot_args caused weird side
  effects in the behavior of the pilot. This commit
  makes sure only the runtime options are taken into
  account and the firecracker-pilot constructs the needed
  boot_args from the runtime section.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 10:51:09 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix race condition

  The race came from stream_io on the host ending the whole session
  when stdin hit EOF, even though the command in the VM was still running.
  Now an early end of input just tells the command its input is over.
  The pilot keeps relaying output until the guest closes the stream,
  and the exit code arrives right after that. The 1s timeout now only
  matters if the connection breaks.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 10:43:45 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix firecracker exit code handling

  So far the exit code of the calling program inside the VM was
  lost in vsock mode. This commit makes sure the exit code is transfered
  via a new vsock port to the caller. This Fixes #176

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 19 21:23:58 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix bwrap lookup in bubblewrwap-pilot

  bubblewrap-pilot checks that bwrap exists by searching PATH,
  but it then runs bwrap from the fixed path /usr/bin/bwrap.
  As such the search doesn't make any sense. This commit
  Fixes #174

