  Applied the change on the documentation side as well.
  This Fixes bsc#1285040

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 19 11:28:42 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add optional egress policy to firecracker network

  flake-ctl firecracker network init now supports the new
  option --egress-deny. The implementation adds a new chain
  FLAKE_PILOT_EGRESS. VM traffic to the outside world now jumps
  from FLAKE_PILOT_FORWARD into the new chain. The new chain
  holds the egress drop rules first. For two prominent
  restrictions the --egress-deny option was simplified:

  * --egress-deny link-local
  * --egress-deny private

  link-local blocks 169.254.0.0/16, which includes the cloud
  metadata service at 169.254.169.254. Without it, a VM reaches
  that service as the host and can read the instance's credentials.
  private blocks the RFC 1918 ranges: 10/8, 172.16/12 and 192.168/16.

  The policy is IPv4 only like the rest of the setup

