Fri Oct 16 12:04:17 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add support for an addon store to podman-pilot

  There is now a new option --use-addon-store to flake-ctl podman pull
  and load. With it set, the image goes into /usr/lib/podman/storage
  and nothing is written to /var/lib/podman/storage. The flag
  is root only because /usr/lib/podman/storage belongs to root
  and consequently this option cannot be used for rootless flakes.
  It's important to know that pruning/deleting of data in the
  additionalstore is not possible with podman because podman treats
  this as read-only. The data there can only be deleted by hand.

