Wed Oct 14 11:10:33 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Volume export/release guest address from state

  flake-ctl firecracker volume export now takes the guest address
  from the allocation file, /var/lib/firecracker/network-state.yaml,
  which belongs to root. It no longer reads the ip= option from
  the flake config. That mattered because in user mode the config
  belongs to the user, who could have put another user's VM address
  there and so had a host path exported to that VM.
  volume release --app uses the same lookup.

