Mon Oct 05 15:10:05 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add /etc/flakes/APP.d drop-in directory

  Users can now put drop-in files in /etc/flakes/APP.d/ to adjust
  system-wide flakes. These files are read last, so their settings
  win. The read order for system wide flakes therefore changes to:

  1. /usr/share/flakes/APP.yaml
  2. /usr/share/flakes/APP.d/* in alphabetical order
  3. /etc/flakes/APP.d/* in alphabetical order

  At registration time an empty drop-in is created in etc/flakes
  and removed on registration remove. A force registration removes
  first and therefore comes back with an empty etc/flakes.

  User registrations under ~/.config/flakes never read /etc/flakes.
  This Fixes #141

