Wed Sep 23 15:45:51 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Add sanity check for NFS server

  If a flake is configured to use NFS volumes but the NFS
  server is not started, the startup of such a flake would
  take a very long time (NFS timeout) and the expected volume
  cannot be attached to the flake. As such a sanity check if
  the nfsd process/thread is running on the host prevents
  users from unknown startup issues.

