Fri Sep 04 10:46:29 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix overlay root (/) permission settings

  sci creates the directories with fs::create_dir_all() which uses
  0777 and let the umask reduce it. At call time of sci no umask
  is set which caused the root (/) to have the wrong permission
  settings. This commit fixes the permissions right after the
  overlay mount and before the switch root.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Sep 04 10:26:18 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Drop use of pivot_root

  sci used the pivot_root (chroot) procedure to switch into the
  new root (/) in case of an overlay root such that sci as a
  process can stay active. This root layout however, can confuse
  applications running on top it. Therefore this commit changes
  the procedure into a standard switch_root followed by a re-exec
  of sci to serve as a real init process.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Sep 04 09:50:48 CEST 2026 - Marcus Schäfer <marcus.schaefer@gmail.com>

- Fix default firecracker setup at registration time

  By default the "flake-ctl firecracker register" call uses a
  firecracker setup template including a network configuraton.
  If a user does not also configure the network via
  "flake-ctl firecracker network add", the call will fail
  because the required tap device is not present. We had
  the --no-net option to avoid this but that's a bad user
  experience. Therefore the default setup now comes without
  a network, meaning the behavior of --no-net is now the
  default procedure and all required steps to add a network
  are part of the firecracker network implementation.

